Id: squid004w
Severity: WARN
Category: services
Check: check_squid
Fix: Keep Safe_ports to what clients need, and http_access deny !Safe_ports.
References: squid.conf.documented
Controls: CIS 4.4; NIST SC-7; ISO 8.20; CE Firewalls

The proxy allows clients but its Safe_ports list is missing, or
holds ports no browsing client needs: mail ports, remote shells and
the like. A client CONNECTs wherever the list allows. Name only the
ports clients need (Squid's defaults: 21, 70, 80, 210, 280, 443,
488, 591, 777 and the unregistered range), and deny the rest first.
Only judged where something is allowed: a proxy that denies
everyone needs no list.
